    {
      "title": "How to start a wash",
      "sectionType": "STEPS",
      "items": [
        {"detail": "Press 전원 (power button) to turn the machine on"},
        {"detail": "Select your program — 표준 세탁 for normal everyday clothes"},
        {"detail": "Pull out the 세제 drawer and add your detergent"},
        {"detail": "Load clothes — do not overfill, keep to about 70% full"},
        {"detail": "Close the door firmly until it clicks"},
        {"detail": "Press 시작 to begin — door locks automatically during the cycle"},
        {"detail": "Never force the door open during a cycle — wait for it to unlock"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Tip",
      "sectionType": "TIP",
      "items": [
        {"detail": "Run 통세척 (drum clean mode) once a month without any clothes inside to prevent mold and bad odors — Korean apartments can be humid. Most machines also have a 세제 clean cycle."}
      ]
